pallets/flask GitHub Discussion #5423

@json_api_dev (opened 2026-03-22)
I'm getting `AttributeError: 'Flask' object has no attribute 'json_encoder'` after upgrading to Flask 3.0. My custom JSONEncoder class was set via `app.json_encoder = CustomEncoder`. How do I migrate?

---

@davidism (Flask maintainer, 2026-03-22)
Flask 3.0 replaced `app.json_encoder` and `app.json_decoder` with a **provider-based system**. Instead of subclassing `JSONEncoder`, you now subclass `flask.json.provider.DefaultJSONProvider`:

```python
from flask.json.provider import DefaultJSONProvider
import datetime

class CustomJSONProvider(DefaultJSONProvider):
    def default(self, o):
        if isinstance(o, datetime.datetime):
            return o.isoformat()
        return super().default(o)

app.json_provider_class = CustomJSONProvider
app.json = CustomJSONProvider(app)
```

Also: `JSON_SORT_KEYS` config is no longer used. Set `app.json.sort_keys = False` on the provider instead. And `flask.json.JSONEncoder` no longer exists — importing it raises `ImportError`.
